    'The square root of D t is a length in the profile, not the depth of a junction. Turning it into a junction depth needs the surface concentration, the background doping and the solid solubility, which are inputs this tool does not take.': 'The square root of D t is a length in the profile, not the depth of a junction. Turning it into a junction depth needs the surface concentration, the background doping and the solid solubility, which are inputs this tool does not take.',
